# A2 Twenty–FullEnrich Enrichment

## Delivery status

**Status:** `DESIGN BASELINE — INTEGRATION AND CONTRACT ACTIVATION PENDING`

This skill records the Step 10 design direction. It does not activate Twenty or FullEnrich, grant write permission, or supersede the active foundation manifest by itself.

## Trigger

Use this skill whenever A2 is asked to retrieve A1-staged Companies from Twenty, assess linked People, use FullEnrich Lookup/Search/Contact Enrichment, select target contacts, or write enrichment results back to Twenty.

## Operating model

- There is no direct A1-to-A2 handoff. A1 stages leads in Twenty.
- Twenty is the operational system of record for Companies, People and associations.
- FullEnrich is the sole enrichment provider for this stage.
- HubSpot, official-site research, Apify and other providers are out of scope.
- A Company may have many linked People. A1 currently inserts at most one; A2 may add up to two new verified primary-target People when no fresh verified primary contact exists.
- Preserve stale or non-primary linked People and mark their status. Never overwrite one human with another human's data.
- Company domain is optional. Its absence must not block an enrichment attempt; use other FullEnrich-supported organisation identifiers and stricter attribution handling.
- The LLM remains the decision-maker. Connector scripts perform deterministic I/O, normalization, asynchronous polling, checkpointing and validated writes only.

## Workflow

1. Resolve the active versions of the Twenty mapping, FullEnrich contract, target-role catalogue, status model, matching policy and write policy.
2. Pull a bounded batch of Companies whose A2 enrichment status is eligible, including all linked People.
3. Claim each Company for the run before any paid provider action.
4. Batch FullEnrich Lookup for linked People requiring verification.
5. Build a compact Lookup decision packet. The LLM decides identity match, Company match, freshness, role priority, retention and whether Search is required.
6. Validate every LLM decision against the packet and active role catalogue.
7. Batch FullEnrich Search only for Companies with no fresh verified primary contact. Search may be domainless when necessary and supported by the verified API contract.
8. Build a compact candidate packet. The LLM may select zero, one or two verified primary-role People; validate IDs, Company attribution, role evidence and deduplication.
9. Batch Contact Enrichment only for selected People, requesting work email and phones. Do not request personal email.
10. Build field-level merge decisions. Values must come from validated provider outputs; protected/manual conflicts are preserved or routed to review.
11. Build and validate an explicit Twenty write plan, then create/update People, create associations and update statuses.
12. Read back the exact Company, People and associations. Only reconciled writes count as success.
13. Finalise Company and Person statuses, audit, provider usage, cost and retry state.

## LLM decision checkpoints

The LLM must reason from compact, schema-validated packets rather than raw provider payloads.

### After Lookup

For each linked Person decide identity status, Company match, exact role and target-role priority, freshness/current-employer status, whether the Person is a usable primary target, and whether People Search is required.

### After Search

For each candidate decide Company attribution, target-role priority, duplicate relationship to existing Twenty People, and retain or reject with rationale. Select at most two new People per Company. A domainless ambiguous match must not be linked automatically.

### Before Twenty write

For each field decide only among: `add`, `update_a2_owned`, `no_change`, `preserve_manual`, `hold_conflict`, `privacy_review`, or `reject_invalid`.

## Connector boundaries

### Twenty connector

- Pull script: metadata-aware filters, pagination, all linked People, snapshots and claims.
- Push script: accepts only a validated write plan; creates/updates People and associations, performs read-back and returns receipts.
- Never embed target-role or candidate-selection reasoning in the connector.

### FullEnrich connector

- People Lookup, People Search and Contact Enrichment are separate scripts.
- Scripts accept bounded arrays and may execute requests concurrently.
- Contact Enrichment handles asynchronous polling internally.
- Scripts return normalized results, provider receipts, terminal states, usage and cost; they never write to Twenty.

## Required contracts

Validate all boundary shapes before implementation: common artifact envelope; Twenty metadata/mapping; Company batch and claim; FullEnrich Lookup/Search/Contact requests and results; LLM decision packets and decisions; Company and Person state models; field merge decisions; Twenty write plan, receipt and reconciliation; run ledger, audit and consumption.

See `references/data-contract-checklist.md` for required invariants.

## Status model

A binary enriched flag is insufficient. Company state should distinguish at least `not_enriched`, `processing`, `enriched`, `partially_enriched`, `completed_no_target`, `retryable_error`, and `blocked`.

Keep Person identity, role/freshness, Company match and contact-enrichment statuses separate. Include policy version, run ID and verification/enrichment timestamps so reruns and stale data can be handled safely.

## Batching and conversation control

- The chat is the orchestration and reasoning plane.
- Batch connector calls, but stop at explicit LLM decision checkpoints.
- Store raw Twenty and FullEnrich responses outside model context; expose compact decision packets with stable IDs and evidence references.
- Bound Companies per chat invocation by context, provider budget and rate limits.
- Persist every stage so an interrupted run can resume without repeating successful paid calls or creating duplicate People.
- Do not run an autonomous end-to-end script that bypasses LLM role, match or retention decisions.

## Verification and stop rules

Stop before a paid call or write when credentials, permissions, mappings, provider request shapes, domainless Search support, budget caps, decision validation, idempotency or audit are unresolved.

Do not claim Twenty write capability based on readable metadata or UI-editable fields. Verify write scope with an approved synthetic record and read-back receipt.

The current live Twenty schema findings are summarized in `references/twenty-live-schema-2026-09.md`. They are an observed integration snapshot, not a permanent field catalogue.

## Pitfalls

- Do not confuse A1's current maximum of one inserted Person with Twenty relationship cardinality.
- Do not require a Company domain; most target organisations lack one.
- Do not reuse A1 discovery, qualification or ICP fields as A2 enrichment state.
- Do not reuse ad-hoc fields such as `wrongpeople` as a workflow state machine.
- Do not let a standalone script make business decisions that belong to the LLM.
- Do not pass raw bulk provider payloads into the chat when a compact decision packet is sufficient.
- Do not mark a Company enriched until all intended Twenty writes reconcile successfully.
